#include <stdio.h>
#include <pthread.h>

// Global mutex for synchronization
pthread_mutex_t logMutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;

void logErrorWithDetails(const char* message, int urgency) {
    // Acquire lock before writing to prevent contention
    pthread_mutex_lock(&logMutex);

    if (urgency > 5) {
        printf("[CRITICAL]: %s\n", message);
    } else {
        printf("[INFO]: %s\n", message);
    }

    // Release lock after writing to allow others to log
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&logMutex);
}
```
This is a simple example that demonstrates how you could start logging errors in a thread-safe manner. It uses a mutex for synchronization, ensuring that only one thread can log at a time to prevent data races. However, this code does not address all of the requirements in your task, such as dynamic limits and integration with external services.

