["Here is a simplified version of such Java Service using Netty for managing persistent connections, Guava EventBus for event driven approach, Jackson for serialization and deserialization, and Javax Validation API for custom data validation. 

Please note that this is just a conceptual model and may need substantial changes to fit into actual requirements.

```Java
import io.netty.bootstrap.Bootstrap;
import io.netty.channel.*;
import io.netty.channel.nio.NioEventLoopGroup;
import io.netty.channel.socket.nio.NioSocketChannel;
import com.google.common.eventbus.EventBus;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper;
import javax.validation.*;
import java.util.Set;

public class RemoteServerService {
    private final EventBus eventBus = new EventBus();
    private final ObjectMapper mapper = new ObjectMapper();
    private final Validator validator = Validation.buildDefaultValidatorFactory().getValidator();

    public void connect(String host, int port) throws InterruptedException {
        EventLoopGroup workerGroup = new NioEventLoopGroup();

        try {
            Bootstrap b = new Bootstrap(); 
            b.group(workerGroup); 
            b.channel(NioSocketChannel.class); 
            b.option(ChannelOption.SO_KEEPALIVE, true); 
            b.handler(new ChannelInitializer<SocketChannel>() {
                @Override
                public void initChannel(SocketChannel ch) throws Exception {
                    ch.pipeline().addLast(new ServerHandler(eventBus, mapper, validator));
                }
            });

            // Start the client.
            ChannelFuture f = b.connect(host, port).sync(); 

            // Wait until the connection is closed.
            f.channel().closeFuture().sync();
        } finally {
            workerGroup.shutdownGracefully();
        }
    }
}

class ServerHandler extends ChannelInboundHandlerAdapter {
    private final EventBus eventBus;
    private final ObjectMapper mapper;
    private final Validator validator;

    public ServerHandler(EventBus eventBus, ObjectMapper mapper, Validator validator) {
        this.eventBus = eventBus;
        this.mapper = mapper;
        this.validator = validator;
    }

    @Override
    public void channelRead(ChannelHandlerContext ctx, Object msg) throws Exception {
        byte[] bytes = (byte[]) msg;

        try {
            CustomData data = mapper.readValue(bytes, CustomData.class);

            Set<ConstraintViolation<CustomData>> violations = validator.validate(data);
            if (!violations.isEmpty()) {
                throw new ConstraintViolationException(violations);
            }

            eventBus.post(new DataReceivedEvent(data));
        } catch (IOException e) {
            // Handle deserialization error here
        }
    }
}
```
This is a simple example, and there are many things you would have to deal with in real-world scenarios such as setting up SSL, handling network partitions, reconnections, etc. Please also note that the configuration for Netty's EventLoopGroup, Bootstrap and its ChannelOptions could be made configurable.
"]

