public class SomeServiceClient {
    private final WebClient webClient;
    private final RetryPolicy retryPolicy = ... //configure a retry policy

    public SomeServiceClient(WebClient.Builder builder, String baseUrl) {
        this.webClient = builder
                .baseUrl(baseUrl)
                .defaultHeader("Authorization", "Bearer " + getToken())
                .build();
    }

    private Mono<SomeResult> callService(String id) {
        return webClient.get()
                .uri("/resource/{id}", id)
                .retrieve()
                .bodyToMono(SomeResult.class)
                .retryWhen(Retry.backoff(3, Duration.ofSeconds(1)) // apply retry policy here
                        .filter(throwable -> throwable instanceof ServiceDownException));
    }
}
```
2) Scaling strategy for worker threads:
```java
public class LoadBalancer {
    private final List<WorkerThread> workers = new ArrayList<>();

    public void addWorker() {
        WorkerThread worker = new WorkerThread(); // create a new worker
        workers.add(worker);
        worker.start();
    }

    public void removeWorker() {
        if (!workers.isEmpty()) {
            WorkerThread worker = workers.remove(0); // remove the first one for example
            worker.stop();
        }
    }
}
```
3) Error handling and fallback:
