```javascript
function dataCollector(stream) {
    let dataArray = []; // Array to store incoming data
    let pauseFlag = false; // Flag to check if the stream should be paused or not

    stream.on('data', (chunk) => {
        if (!pauseFlag) { // If not paused, save the chunk to the array
            dataArray.push(chunk);
        }
    });

    function pause() { // Function to pause the stream
        pauseFlag = true;
    };

    function resume() { // Function to resume the stream
        pauseFlag = false;
    };

    return { 
        data: () => dataArray, // Getter for the data array
        pause: pause, // Pause function
        resume: resume, // Resume function
    }
};
```
In this example, `dataCollector` takes a stream as input and returns an object with three methods - `data()` to get the current state of the collected data array, `pause()` to pause the stream from adding new chunks to the array, and `resume()` to resume the stream again.

Please consider contacting me if you need more help on a specific section or aspect of this project.
