['This is a complex task which involves several components such as distributed processing frameworks like Apache Kafka or Apache Samza, Java concurrency utilities for locking mechanisms, distributed consensus algorithms like Raft or Paxos, an external service integrations using REST APIs or gRPC, real-time anomaly detection, integration with various external systems and more. 

This is a high level abstract of what your application could look like. Please note that it does not provide full code but the general idea on how to start:

```java
public class DynamicLogProcessor {
    private final Lock lock;
    private final ConsensusAlgorithm consensusAlgorithm;
    private final LogTransformer logTransformer;
    private final StorageService storageService;
    private final NotificationService notificationService;
    private final MetadataAPI metadataAPI;

    public DynamicLogProcessor(Lock lock, ConsensusAlgorithm consensusAlgorithm, 
            LogTransformer logTransformer, StorageService storageService, 
            NotificationService notificationService, MetadataAPI metadataAPI) {
        this.lock = lock;
        this.consensusAlgorithm = consensusAlgorithm;
        this.logTransformer = logTransformer;
        this.storageService = storageService;
        this.notificationService = notificationService;
        this.metadataAPI = metadataAPI;
    }

    public void processLogs(LogBatch logBatch) {
        if (consensusAlgorithm.isPrimary()) {
            logBatch = logTransformer.transform(logBatch);
            storageService.save(logBatch);
            notificationService.notify();
            metadataAPI.enrich(logBatch);
        } else {
            consensusAlgorithm.validateAndRefine(logBatch);
            lock.acquire();
            try {
                storageService.commit(logBatch);
                notificationService.acknowledge();
                metadataAPI.confirm(logBatch);
            } finally {
                lock.release();
            }
        }
    }
}
```
The above code is a simplified version of the application and does not handle all aspects described in the task such as load balancing, failover, adaptive backoff strategies, unit tests, documentation, integration with external systems, real-time anomaly detection or dynamic adjustment. 

