            while ((count = in.read(buffer)) > 0) {
                md.update(buffer, 0, count);
            }

            byte[] hashBytes = md.digest();
            StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
            for (byte b : hashBytes) {
                sb.append(String.format("%02x", b));
            }
            System.out.println("Hash for " + path + " is: " + sb);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // Handle your exceptions here 
        }
    }

    // Implement other features like remote file access, concurrent processing, etc...
}
```
For Union-Find data structure implementation and supporting complex, distributed file processing pipeline, you may need to consider using frameworks such as Apache Hadoop or Spark for big data processing. Configuring the hash algorithm can be done using environment variables with System.getenv() or a property file reader like java.util.Properties or Apache Commons Configuration. Logging and error handling are often handled by logging frameworks, e.g., log4j or SLF4J, respectively. 

