['Below is an example of how this could be implemented in PHP using PDO for database interactions, GuzzleHttp/Client for API calls and Symfony's Cache Component for caching. Note that creating an actual user account management system would involve much more code and complexity as it also involves other functionalities like login, session management, password recovery etc.

Please replace the placeholders with your real values for external service details. 

```php
<?php
require 'vendor/autoload.php';
use GuzzleHttp\Client;
use Symfony\Component\Cache\Adapter\FilesystemAdapter;
use Symfony\Component\Cache\Psr16Cache;

class UserAccountManager {
    private $dbh;
    private $cache;
    private $authService;

    public function __construct() {
        $this->dbh = new PDO('mysql:host=localhost;dbname=test', $user, $pass);
        $pool = new FilesystemAdapter();
        $this->cache = new Psr16Cache($pool);

        $this->authService = new Client([
            'base_uri' => 'https://api.externalauthenticationservice.com/',
            'headers' => [
                'X-Api-Key' => 'your_real_key_here',
            ],
        ]);
    }

    public function createUser($email, $password) {
        $hashedPassword = password_hash($password, PASSWORD_DEFAULT);

        // Check if user exists and handle accordingly
        $stmt = $this->dbh->prepare('INSERT INTO users (email, password) VALUES (?, ?)');
        $stmt->execute([$email, $hashedPassword]);
        $userId = $this->dbh->lastInsertId();

        // Call external service for token generation
        $response = $this->authService->post('tokens', [
            'json' => ['user_id' => $userId]
        ]);
        $token = json_decode($response->getBody(), true)['token'];

        // Cache the user data for quick access 
        $this->cache->set('user.'.$userId, [
            'email' => $email,
            'password' => $hashedPassword,
            'token' => $token
        ]);

        return $this->formatResponse("User account successfully created", "success", [
            'user_id' => $userId, 
            'email' => $email, 
            'token' => $token
        ]);
    }

    public function updateUser($userId, $newEmail, $newPassword) {
        $hashedNewPassword = password_hash($newPassword, PASSWORD_DEFAULT);

        // Update user in database
        $stmt = $this->dbh->prepare('UPDATE users SET email = ?, password = ? WHERE id = ?');
        $stmt->execute([$newEmail, $hashedNewPassword, $userId]);

        // Update cache 
        $cachedUser = $this->cache->getItem('user.'.$userId);
        $cachedUser->set(['email' => $newEmail, 'password' => $hashedNewPassword]);
        $this->cache->save($cachedUser);

        return $this->formatResponse("User account successfully updated", "success", [
            'user_id' => $userId, 
            'email' => $newEmail
        ]);
    }

    public function deleteUser($userId) {
        $stmt = $this->dbh->prepare('DELETE FROM users WHERE id = ?');
        $stmt->execute([$userId]);

        // Invalidate cache 
        $this->cache->deleteItem('user.'.$userId);

        return $this->formatResponse("User account successfully deleted", "success");
    }

    private function formatResponse($message, $status, $data = []) {
        return json_encode([
            'status' => $status,
            'message' => $message,
            'data' => $data
        ]);
    }
}
?>
```
This is a basic example and does not cover all the constraints specified. It does not include data validation, error handling or logging. Implementing these would require additional complexity and need to be added as per your project requirements. This also needs to be adapted for real usage by providing proper exception handling and input sanitization.
']

